      p: ['A sheep’s or goat’s ankle bone, thrown, comes to rest on one of its four long sides; it will not stand on its rounded ends. In ancient Greece and Rome the four sides were given the values 1, 3, 4 and 6, and four bones were thrown together.', 'The two broad sides come up often and the two narrow ones seldom. That is the difference from a cubic die, whose faces all come up alike.'],
